From 3fcb3190515ba3643e001a42e5f62a17b6dbd7c7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex Unleashed <codex-unleashed@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 01:09:49 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Use a mountable procfs denial to test snapshot descriptor
 fallback

Tracks https://github.com/holdmyspot-com/codex-unleashed/issues/49.

The blocked-descriptor replay case denies /dev/fd. In the sandbox, /dev/fd is
the symlink that bubblewrap's --dev creates to /proc/self/fd, so masking it
with tmpfs follows the symlink, fails with ENOENT and bubblewrap exits before
Bash starts. On Linux the test now denies /proc, which removes the descriptor
path the same way, and runs its exec-server in the caller's PID namespace so
that no fresh /proc is mounted over the denial. The replay profile now fails
if Bash sourced the snapshot through /dev/fd, so the test proves the fallback
ran. macOS keeps the /dev/fd denial.

Declared base: openai/codex main dddc3c0a79528c4de8d9a20d51dd3bd89b02a3e4.
---
 codex-rs/exec-server/tests/common/mod.rs      |  5 ++++
 .../tests/exec_process/shell_snapshot.rs      | 26 ++++++++++++++++---
 2 files changed, 27 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/codex-rs/exec-server/tests/common/mod.rs b/codex-rs/exec-server/tests/common/mod.rs
